<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA- COMMISSION APPROVES BUTINGES LOAN GUARANTEE.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA- COMMISSION APPROVES BUTINGES LOAN GUARANTEE.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's state foreign loans commission on Friday approved a $10 million loan guarantee to the Butinges oil terminal project from the Union bank of Switzerland, the Ministry of European Affairs said in a statement.</p>
<p>The government recently said that it would reduce its majority stake in the financially troubled oil terminal project to a minority.</p>
<p>The company has had difficulty securing loans and attracting investors.</p>
<p>Analysts say that the terminal's viability is questionable when the oil terminal in the Latvian port of Ventspils is operating at only 50 percent of its capacity.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
